---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="For Commercial Explorers — AI Resource Exploration"
  description="AI-augmented mineral targeting built for geologists who have to defend the discovery — NI 43-101 and JORC-aligned outputs, founded on 30 years of field practice."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-geo-slate text-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center" data-reveal>
      <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-5">For Commercial Explorers</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl text-white leading-[1.08] mb-6">
        Built for the geologist who has to defend the discovery.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-prose mx-auto">
        CAGE-IN delivers ranked exploration target portfolios referenced to peer-reviewed deposit models — outputs structured for NI 43-101 and JORC-aligned reporting, authored by a founder with 30 years of multidisciplinary field experience across 60+ projects in 20+ countries. If your board is asking why these targets and not those, this is the tool that gives you the answer in writing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- In-development callout -->
  <section class="py-12 md:py-20 bg-geo-deep">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="border border-dashed border-white/15 rounded-xl p-10 text-center bg-white/[0.02]" data-reveal>
        <p class="text-geo-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">In Development</p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-white mb-4">Page in development</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-prose mx-auto mb-6">
          This page will cover CAGE-IN's output specification for NI 43-101 and JORC workflows, the founder's 60+ project track record across five continents, performance benchmarks for listed-explorer budgets, and how AI-backed fluid software keeps your prospectivity model current as the peer-reviewed literature evolves — not frozen at the date of delivery.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="inline-block px-8 py-3.5 rounded bg-geo-gold text-white font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider hover:bg-amber-500 transition-colors"
        >
          Get in touch in the meantime →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</PageLayout>
